      "writtenOn": "2020-05-26T23:42:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the right region to use, but it will conflict with the region I chose for rollback: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/a1c00f79e0a2aab2731777fe7a7c3c80ddb3869b/core/cortex-m/mpu.c#329\n\nIt looks like REGION_CODE_RAM may be unused, so we could change rollback to use that if it\u0027s unused.\n\nAlso, can you double-check the existing logic in mpu_config_region? It tries to use subregions if the size is not a power of two and can end up using one value higher than the region specified: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/a1c00f79e0a2aab2731777fe7a7c3c80ddb3869b/core/cortex-m/mpu.c#169\n\nThis is where the comment in the num about \"Second region for unaligned size\" comes from I think: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/a1c00f79e0a2aab2731777fe7a7c3c80ddb3869b/core/cortex-m/include/mpu.h#29\n\nHere are the details on subregions:\n\nhttps://developer.arm.com/docs/dui0553/a/cortex-m4-peripherals/optional-memory-protection-unit/mpu-region-attribute-and-size-register\n\nhttps://developer.arm.com/docs/dui0553/a/cortex-m4-peripherals/optional-memory-protection-unit/updating-an-mpu-region#BIHEEIGC",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 276,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "a1c00f79e0a2aab2731777fe7a7c3c80ddb3869b",
